    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερβᾰσ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>passover,</i> given as equiv. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάσχα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				2.14.6
			</span></i>: but commonly, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., <i>transgression, trespass,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερβασίῃ Διὸς ὅρκια δηλήσηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.107
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίσασθαι μνηστῆρας ὑ. ἀλεγεινῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.206
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεάν, Ζεῦ, δύνασιν τίς ἀνδρῶν ὑ.
					κατάσχοι;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					605
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): pl., <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.589
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.168
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				828
			</span></i>.</div>
